m chief bell stated that  officers have been going from truck to  truck to advise individuals that they  are participating in an illegal  demonstration  and they have made it crystal clear  that if the illegal demonstrators do not  leave  they will face serious consequences  interim chief bell has also confirmed  that he is confident that the ottawa  police service and the integrated  command unit have the appropriate  resources authorities that they require  and a  very concrete plan to move forward  he emphasized that this operation will  not be considered complete  until the streets are cleared  and that peace and order has been fully  restored  to the good people of the city of ottawa  to the individuals who continue to  participate in this illegal occupation  it's time to go home  now  and to those who have children with them  this is no place for children take them  home immediately take them to a place of  safety  the ottawa police service and their  partners have engaged the planning team  with the children's aid society to  encourage anyone with children in the  area  to leave immediately and to take their  kids to some place safe  to the people of ottawa i want to assure  you  we will continue to work and support  with our municipal and provincial  partners  to make sure that this occupation ends  safely and swiftly and respectful of  charter rights and freedoms and  upholding the rule of law  so that they can get their city back and  they can get their lives back  the decision to invoke the emergency act  was one as the deputy prime minister  said that we took with great caution and  care  and i will share with you as she did  we approached it even with sincere  regret  regret that this was necessary  but make no mistake we were resolved to  do what was required  to uphold the rule of law  to protect protect canadians interests  and to defend our country our democratic  institutions  and our the people of this country we  know that it was necessary  to give law enforcement and our other  officials the tools authorities and  resources that they require to do the  job  and i want to assure all canadians we  will not hesitate to do whatever is  required to protect our ports of entry  to protect canadian interests from the  criminal intent of people behind these  blockades  and to restore  peace and order in our country  and finally to the people and residents  of ottawa i want to acknowledge how they  have suffered  from threats of threats and intimidation  from acts that were clearly intended to  greater bring the greatest disruption to  the lives  of their fellow citizens  and indeed all canadians i want to  assure them that this will end  and that we  will be there for them to continue to  support them and to hold those  who have taken from them  the peace of their of their  neighborhoods and their communities we  will hold them to account for their  actions thank you all very much merci  beaucoup um i would like to invite uh  people who may have questions of myself  and my colleagues please proceed  from journalists until 11 55 and we'll  start in the room  hi it's annie bergeron oliver with ctv  national news my question is for you  minister freeland you mentioned in your  opening remarks that action is being  taken by financial services and that's  making a difference i'm wondering if you  can provide any specific numbers on how  many accounts either personal or  corporate are being targeted  and also what type of safeguards are in  place to ensure that it's protesters and  not simply someone with the same name  whose accounts are being targeted and  frozen  uh well thank you very much for the  question  i have those numbers here in front of me  and they were reviewed just last night  by me  and minister mendicino minister blair  the prime minister and minister lametty  but i'm not going to share them  with you right now because operational  actions are being taken and we want to  be very very careful not to jeopardize  those operational actions but i do want  to assure you and through you all  canadians  that action is being taken  we are seeing it  and that action is going to increase in  the coming days  um  it's a good question about  uh  what are the safeguards and there i  really want to assure all canadians that  that is something very much on our minds  that is something that  we  and law enforcement and the financial  service providers have been working on  very very carefully and that's why i say  the financial the use of the financial  tools is actually going to increase in  the coming days because it was important  for us to be sure that safeguards were  in place  and i do also want to say  that  the actions we have taken  are emergency measures  due process  remains in place  charter rights  remain in place  and of course  the courts  are there  and they will be these will all be  institutions that will be there to  support canadians  okay so my follow-up is in two parts  then so you're confirming that accounts  have been frozen both personal and  corporate but you're not releasing the  information and the actual follow-up is  i'm just wondering whether the bank  accounts will be targeted of individuals  who donated to the give sengo and the  gofundme campaigns are they considered  designated people under the emergencies  act meaning that their credit cards  could be cut and financial services are  targeting them as well  okay so  the names of both individuals and  entities  as well as crypto wallets  have been shared  by the rcmp  with financial institutions  and accounts have been frozen  and more accounts will be frozen  a  crowd funding platforms and payment  service providers have started the  registration process  with  fintrac  uh in terms of the specifics on whose  accounts are being frozen  you now  have  the regulations  the financial service providers have  those regulations as well  and they working with law enforcement  will be making the operational decisions  but i do want to say really clearly to  canadians  we have now outlined with great clarity  that these blockades and occupations are  illegal  it is now time for people to go home  to take their trucks home  and to stop funding  illegal blockades and occupations  yes alex balingal with the toronto star  um just on the same subject  the warning that you're issuing to the  drivers about their accounts being  suspended and their truck insurance  being suspended is pretty unequivocal so  i'm wondering if you can say uh  or shed some light on whether the to  what degree i guess the fine the large  financial institutions are actually on  board with this and also uh clarify  exactly why you can't share  the figures why that's an operational  secret at this point  the  emergencies act  has  compelled financial service providers  to take these actions  and we have provided them  with immunity for actions undertaken in  good faith under these measures  those are two important facts  the financial service providers  have a stake in canada and the canadian  economy  and  they  are  a really important institutional pillar  of canada  they are as they are legally obliged to  do  collaborating properly and effectively  with the rcmp  with law and with law enforcement  in terms of disclosing specifics  um  all of us uh had a conversation  yesterday with law enforcement about  that  and  there was a clear view  that it's important right now  not to in any way jeopardize  the very important work law enforcement  is taking and that's why i'm not  disclosing the specifics but let me  assure you  those details  will be disclosed  in due course and soon  and and i want you to know it is  happening i do have the numbers in front  of me and  i do particularly want  people who are participating in illegal  blockades and an illegal occupation to  know  these measures  are real  they are being used  they will have an impact  and there is a really easy way  to avoid being affected by these  measures and that is  just go home  go back to work  um and i think that minister mendocino  you mentioned that um you know all the  border crossings that have been  blockaded are cleared there's been  attempts i guess to re-blockade them  um and then that's been part of the  justification you you guys have used for  the emergencies act  but you've also mentioned that you want  to  lift this emergency declaration before  the 30-day limit is up so i if you if  the concern is them returning what are  the conditions you need to see  i guess as a government as a cabinet in  order to actually lift this emergency  declaration um well  first and foremost uh one of the  conditions is that  the blockades uh are no longer  there and that is one of the reasons why  we have been going to great pains over  the last number of days to send a very  clear unequivocal message to those uh  who are  participating in them be they at a  border or in front of a legislature  including here  in ottawa in front of the parliament but  equally in in the communities and in the  neighborhoods where these are no longer  just mere disturbances of the peace  where there has been a rampant and  flagrant disregard for the law the time  is now to stop  and to go home  and you've heard me say it you've heard  mr blair say it you've heard the deputy  prime minister say it you've heard the  prime minister say it you've heard  yesterday the interim  ottawa police chief said  there should be no ambiguity right now  to anyone that is still participating in  an illegal blockade  whether it's for  some misguided under the misguided  belief that this is a lawful protest  when it is not or for some other uh more  malevolent purpose the time is to go  home  and the invocation of the emergencies  act  is a resort that we came to  as a result of the significant  challenges that law enforcement using  conventional tools had faced for the  last three weeks  and while we have made progress  while we see that the ports of entry are  open right now um i would suggest that  at this fragile moment it's precarious i  mean yesterday you just heard  mayor drew dilkins in the course of a  press conference say that there was yet  another effort to try and shut it down  again  and so yes i mean i think we all want to  be cautiously optimistic that we are  coming to the end of it um but in the  meantime as a government  we have an obligation and a  responsibility to canadians to make sure  that we are using all of the tools in  the box  and yes that includes declaring certain  areas as no-go zones that includes the  ability to commandeer the kind of assets  that are required to  preserve the flow of traffic at our at  our critical infrastructure including at  our borders um that includes choking off  proceeds currencies that may be used to  advance the illegal blockade and in the  case of the rcmp  that includes using a very um important  and time limited measure to be able to  rapidly deploy them so that we can  ensure that there is public safety so  you know  we're getting there but we're not quite  there yet and obviously it is our desire  to  see the  the measures that we have introduced  under the order sunset as quickly as  possible but that will be a decision  that is taken again very carefully on  the advice of our officials on the  advice of law enforcement and what we're  seeing and hearing on the ground  thanks we'll take one more question in  the room and then take questions from  the phone not questions  uh  on the frozen accounts  you have the operational  responsibilities to implement  but i can assure you  that  to this point there have been  accounts that have been frozen it is an  ongoing process  that will accelerate  [Music]  [Music]  that there  from extremists  institutions or democratic constitutions  and our economy  for questions over the phone please  press star one on the devices keypad  okay  being adopted  [Music]  existing methods  currently existing in canada  they are completely illegal  and completely constitutional  for us  there's a debate of the house of commons  that the house of commons participate  that it votes  on this is  completely essential  our goal  is the democratic institutions of canada  and we will proceed  absolutely  absolutely  to take  uh  it is a very delicate situation for  everybody  but the measures that are included in  the destination  all those reasons that the government  has to canadians  and  questions  thank you  so much  as a follower  my question was more when would you want  to see the house  [Music]  emergencies act it's a technical  question it's a question that the chef  uh  house leader uh delay at least  opposition we'll be discussing uh with  other  house leaders  that there are weapons  what are the plans to ensure that they  clarification i'm not saying that there  is an intelligence saying that there are  weapons  inaudible question inaudible to the  international  answer it's an important point  as i said yesterday  legislators  and there's a similarity in the rhetoric  the social media  emerging in social media and elsewhere  those are similarities that everybody  is sharing concerns about  questions  so here you're telling me that there are  no weapons in ottawa  okay  that was my follow-up question  my follow-up question was about the  children who are in downtown ottawa  some people protesters are calling for  more children to come so that children  so that the police will be impeded in  their actions  the firearms and all the risks that's  the question for the police services  there's a difference between our  different functions here  it is  create legislation to enact it  responsibility  related  we're emphasizing that they need to go  the kids need to go now  thank you very much you're done okay  unfortunately we really have to cut it  off they have to get going yeah i i  think i think we i we're joining  minister blair for the debate um but  we'll be h